<title>GERMANY: Pan-German March industry orders rise 1.1 pct m/m.</title>
<headline>Pan-German March industry orders rise 1.1 pct m/m.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The economics ministry reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p> PAN-GERMAN INDUSTRY ORDERS  Mar 97     Feb 97     Mar 96</p>
<p> Month-on-month change	  +1.1	 -0.2	 +1.4</p>
<p> Year-on-year		     +5.5	 +5.8	 -3.5</p>
<p> Index (base 1991)		99.7	 98.6	 94.5</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures are seasonally adjusted and provisional and expressed in volume terms. Year-on-year changes are calculated by Reuters from Bundesbank data.  </p>
<p>The ministry gave the following month-on-month details:</p>
<p>				     Mar 97     Feb 97   Mar 97 index</p>
<p> Total domestic orders	  +0.7	 +1.1	  90.0</p>
<p> Total foreign orders	   +2.0	 -2.4	 119.1</p>
<p> Intermediate goods	     +1.1	 +2.3	 103.0</p>
<p> Of which: domestic	     +0.5	 +2.6	  94.3</p>
<p>	     foreign		+2.2	 +1.3	 123.0</p>
<p> Capital goods		    +1.0	 -3.7	  99.8</p>
<p> Of which: domestic	     +0.9	 -1.5	  88.5</p>
<p>	     foreign		+0.9	 -6.2	 118.1</p>
<p> Consumer goods, durables     +1.3	 +0.1	  91.3</p>
<p> Of which: domestic	     -0.2	 +2.0	  81.3</p>
<p>	     foreign		+3.9	 -2.8	 112.0</p>
<p>Two-month comparison Feb/Mar 97 with Dec/Jan 96/97:</p>
<p> Industrial orders		     +1.5</p>
<p> Domestic orders			 +1.0</p>
<p> Foreign orders			  +2.5</p>
<p> Intermediate goods		    +2.5</p>
<p> Capital goods			   +1.0</p>
<p> Consumer goods, durables	    +1.0</p>
<p>Two month comparison Feb/Mar 97 with Feb/Mar 96:</p>
<p> Industrial orders		     +0.9</p>
<p> Domestic orders			 -2.3</p>
<p> Foreign orders			  +6.1</p>
<p> Intermediate goods		    +4.9</p>
<p> Capital goods			   -3.3</p>
<p> Consumer goods, durables	    -0.9</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097-150</p>
</text>
